  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">National Expert - DG ECHO, Bryssel - National Expert - DG ECHO, Bryssel, AG</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Nationell Expert - DG ECHO, Bryssel</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The position is based within the unit&apos;s team for quality and efficiency in humanitarian financing. The national expert will strengthen the team across the unit&#x2019;s entire policy work, including strategic priorities such as the humanitarian-development-peace nexus in fragile settings, initiatives to bridge the funding gap (innovative financing, efficiency gains through quality funding), promotion of cash-based assistance, and the localization agenda. The role will provide analysis on these topics, including political developments in the Member States, and contribute to advancing policy guidance internally and within the relevant Directorates-General. The position will particularly serve as the focal point for overall relations with DG INTPA and DG NEAR</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Tj&#xe4;nsten &#xe4;r placerad inom enhetens team f&#xf6;r kvalitet och effektivitet inom humanit&#xe4;r finansiering. Den nationella experten kommer att f&#xf6;rst&#xe4;rka teamet inom hela enhetens policyverksamhet, inklusive strategiska prioriteringar som kopplingen mellan humanit&#xe4;rt bist&#xe5;nd, utveckling och fred i instabila milj&#xf6;er, initiativ f&#xf6;r att &#xf6;verbrygga finansieringsgapet (innovativ finansiering, effektivitetsvinster genom kvalitetsfinansiering), fr&#xe4;mjande av kontanter och lokaliseringsagendan. Tj&#xe4;nsten kommer att tillhandah&#xe5;lla analyser av dessa &#xe4;mnen, inklusive den politiska utvecklingen i medlemsstaterna, och bidra till att fr&#xe4;mja de politiska riktlinjerna internt och inom ber&#xf6;rda generaldirektorat. Tj&#xe4;nsten kommer s&#xe4;rskilt att fungera som kontaktpunkt f&#xf6;r de &#xf6;vergripande relationerna med GD INTPA och GD MENA.</narrative>
  </description>
